ull,"decoding":null,"altVerdict":"GOOD","altReason":"present, no red flags","bytes":33190}]},"standards":{"engine":"standards","checks":[{"id":"schema-gov","label":"schema.org GovernmentOrganization markup","pass":false,"detail":""},{"id":"canonical","label":"Canonical URL declared","pass":true,"detail":""},{"id":"hreflang","label":"hreflang alternates declared","pass":false,"detail":""},{"id":"title","label":"Page has a <title>","pass":true,"detail":""},{"id":"description","label":"Meta description present","pass":true,"detail":""},{"id":"charset","label":"Character encoding declared","pass":true,"detail":""},{"id":"lang","label":"Document language (lang) set","pass":true,"detail":"en"},{"id":"viewport","label":"Responsive viewport (zoom not disabled)","pass":true,"detail":"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0"},{"id":"open-graph","label":"Open Graph tags (5/6)","pass":true,"detail":""},{"id":"twitter-card","label":"Twitter card metadata","pass":true,"detail":""},{"id":"open-social","label":"Open social presence (Mastodon/Bluesky) linked","pass":false,"detail":""}],"passed":8,"total":11,"social":[],"og":{"title":"Center for Advanced Subsurface Earth Resource Models (CASERM)","description":"The Center to Advance the Science of Exploration to Reclamation in Mining (CASERM) aims to transform the way that geoscience data are used in the mineral resource industry. Research focuses on the integration of diverse geoscience data to improve decision-making across the mine life cycle, beginning with exploration for subsurface earth resources and continuing through mine operation as well as closure and environmental remediation. CASERM also addresses the critical need for training and preparation of graduates and young professionals by educating the next generation of scientists and engineers working in the mining sector. The Center’s vision is to become a globally recognized center of excellence, spearheading the future of mineral discovery, extraction, and reclamation.CASERM focuses on the research and development needs of the mining industry, which provides the building blocks on which the U.S. economy depends. Precompetitive research within CASERM serves an industrial sector that currently produces minerals and materials valued at $90.4 billion per year (U.S. Geological Survey 2022) and provides direct employment for 181,000 miners, geologists, and mining engineers (U.S. Bureau of Labor Statistics 2022). With the value added through processing of the raw materials, activities within CASERM impact an industry that accounts for ~15% of the nation’s gross domestic product (U.S. Geological Survey 2022).","url":"/centers/center-for-advanced-subsurface-earth-resource-models/","image":"/assets/images/twittercard.png","siteName":null,"type":"article"},"resilience":{"checks":[{"id":"pwa-https","label":"HTTPS (required for service workers)","status":"pass","evidence":"","exampleUrl":"https://iucrc.nsf.gov/centers/center-for-advanced-subsurface-earth-resource-models/","why":"HTTPS is required for service workers and most install prompts."},{"id":"pwa-manifest","label":"Web app manifest declared","status":"fail","evidence":"","exampleUrl":"https://iucrc.nsf.gov/centers/center-for-advanced-subsurface-earth-resource-models/","why":"A web app manifest is required for installability and controls how the app appears when launched."},{"id":"pwa-service-worker","label":"Service worker registered","status":"fail","evidence":"","exampleUrl":"https://iucrc.nsf.gov/centers/center-for-advanced-subsurface-earth-resource-models/","why":"A service worker is what makes offline access, caching, and background sync possible."},{"id":"pwa-theme-color","label":"Theme color declared","status":"fail","evidence":"","exampleUrl":"https://iucrc.nsf.gov/centers/center-for-advanced-subsurface-earth-resource-models/","why":"Theme color controls the browser chrome/status-bar color when the site is installed or bookmarked."},{"id":"pwa-apple-touch-icon","label":"Apple touc